                                        Group Management

--> in linux group help us organize users and set permission for specific resources.
--> we can control access based on the group

groupadd <group_name>
--> to create group
groupadd aws

groupdel <group_name>
--> to delete group
groupdel aws

/etc/group = stored group related information

/etc/group file contains:

aws  :  x  :  5003  :  
 1      2       3     4

 1 : group name
 2 : group password
 3 : group ID
 4 : list of group members

 **Type of groups:
 1. Primary group
 --> the user's main/default group
 2. Secondary group
 --> additional groups the user belongs to

 usermod -aG <group_name> <user_name>
 --> append single user
 usermod -aG aws seema

 gpasswd -M <user1>,<user2>,<user3>....  <group_name>
 --> to add multiple users at a time
 gpasswd -M priya,atul aws

 gpasswd -d <user_name> <group_name>
 --> to delete user from group
 gpasswd -d amit aws

 groupmod -n <group_new_name> <old_group_name>
 --> to update group name
 groupmod -n devops aws

 

